libpsl is a C library for the Public Suffix List (PSL). The PSL is a list of
domain name suffixes under which internet users can directly register domain
names, maintained by Mozilla at publicsuffix.org. It is widely used by
browsers and HTTP clients to enforce cookie scoping and same-origin policies.

This KOS port compiles the built-in DAFSA-encoded PSL data from the release
tarball, requiring no external data files or Unicode libraries at runtime.

URL: https://rockdaboot.github.io/libpsl
